      "revision": 1355861250,
      "text": "Salvia fruticosa, or Greek sage, is a perennial herb or sub-shrub native to the eastern Mediterranean, including Southern Italy, the Canary Islands and North Africa. It is especially abundant in Palestine, Israel, and Lebanon."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Salvia fruticosa",
